{"jurisdiction":"MI","generatedAt":"2026-11-05T05:54:04Z","bills":{"MI-2025-HB6442":{"id":"MI-2025-HB6442","passed":false,"number":"HB 6442","title":"Labor: health and safety; occupational health standards related to exposure to work in hot environments; require director to promulgate. Amends 1974 PA 154 (MCL 408.1001 - 408.1094) by adding sec. 14s.","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-10-28","sponsor":{"name":"Carrie Rheingans","party":"D","state":"MI","district":"47"},"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-11-05","text":"bill electronically reproduced 10/28/2026","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-28","text":"introduced by Representative Rep. Carrie Rheingans","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-28","text":"read a first time","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-28","text":"referred to Committee on Government Operations","chamber":"House"}],"law":null,"policyArea":"Labor: health and safety","url":"https://legislature.mi.gov/Bills/Bill?ObjectName=2026-HB-6442","textUrl":"https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2025-2026/billintroduced/House/htm/2026-HIB-6442.htm","versions":[{"label":"House Introduced Bill","date":null,"url":"https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2025-2026/billintroduced/House/htm/2026-HIB-6442.htm","type":"HTML"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The bill would require the state labor director to set workplace safety rules for workers exposed to heat or hot work areas. The rules would cover employer heat plans, indoor and outdoor heat checks, water and rest breaks at set temperature levels, worker training, reporting heat illnesses and deaths, and protection from retaliation for reporting heat hazards. It would also allow some employers to be exempt and require the director to publish the reported data.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"MI-2025-HB6435":{"id":"MI-2025-HB6435","passed":false,"number":"HB 6435","title":"Civil procedure: civil actions; cause of action for deed fraud; provide for. Amends 1961 PA 236 (MCL 600.101 - 600.9947) by adding sec. 2980.","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-10-21","sponsor":{"name":"Tonya Phillips","party":"D","state":"MI","district":"7"},"cosponsors":[{"name":"Kara Hope","party":"D","state":"MI","date":null,"withdrawn":false}],"cosponsorCount":1,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-10-28","text":"bill electronically reproduced 10/21/2026","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-21","text":"introduced by Representative Rep. Tonya Myers Phillips","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-21","text":"read a first time","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-21","text":"referred to Committee on Judiciary","chamber":"House"}],"law":null,"policyArea":"Civil procedure: civil actions, Property: recording","url":"https://legislature.mi.gov/Bills/Bill?ObjectName=2026-HB-6435","textUrl":"https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2025-2026/billintroduced/House/htm/2026-HIB-6435.htm","versions":[{"label":"House Introduced Bill","date":null,"url":"https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2025-2026/billintroduced/House/htm/2026-HIB-6435.htm","type":"HTML"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The bill would let a person who was a victim of deed theft sue in circuit court over real property taken without their approval or through fraud. If they win, they could recover $5,000, three times their actual losses, and reasonable lawyer fees. It would affect owners of residential or commercial property, and it would take effect 90 days after becoming law.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"MI-2025-SB712":{"id":"MI-2025-SB712","passed":false,"number":"SB 712","title":"Courts: district court; magistrate qualifications; modify. Amends secs. 8501 & 8507 of 1961 PA 236 (MCL 600.8501 & 600.8507).","summary":null,"summarySour